\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Federated GAT-CTDE, per-seed evidence. (a) Paired per-seed federation cost on mean reward per step (same 10 seeds): centralized training scores higher on 6 seeds, federated on 3, with 1 tie -- a real but borderline-significant edge (Wilcoxon $p=0.055$), shown as individual seed trajectories rather than two independent bars, since the significance test itself is paired. (b) Privacy-utility curve using block precision, the metric that survives the compliance-based curve's non-monotonic, uninterpretable pattern at the same noise levels: individual seed values (light dots) are shown behind the mean, along with the seed count that ever blocked anything at each $\sigma $ (precision is undefined otherwise) -- precision is perfect through $\sigma =1.0$ and drops sharply by $\sigma =4.0$.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:m3-privacy}{{4}{6}{}{}{}}
